## SQ-STN-03 | Pickling Jar progress restarts when the recipe changes; kimchi only after its full time
> zq rdetail pickle_from_fermenting
> zq rdetail kimchi_from_onion
> setblock 300 -60 340 vintagedelight:fermenting_jar{inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"vintagedelight:cucumber",Count:1b},{Slot:1,id:"vintagedelight:cucumber",Count:1b},{Slot:2,id:"vintagedelight:cucumber",Count:1b},{Slot:3,id:"vintagedelight:cucumber",Count:1b},{Slot:4,id:"vintagedelight:cucumber",Count:1b},{Slot:5,id:"vintagedelight:salt_dust",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 70
> zc2 inv 300 -60 340
> data merge block 300 -60 340 {inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"farmersdelight:cabbage_leaf",Count:1b},{Slot:1,id:"farmersdelight:cabbage_leaf",Count:1b},{Slot:2,id:"farmersdelight:cabbage_leaf",Count:1b},{Slot:3,id:"farmersdelight:cabbage_leaf",Count:1b},{Slot:4,id:"vintagedelight:salt_dust",Count:1b},{Slot:5,id:"farmersdelight:onion",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 1
> zc2 inv 300 -60 340
sleep 100
> zc2 inv 300 -60 340
sleep 21
> zc2 inv 300 -60 340
reject \[zc2\] error
look (1) rdetail: pickle_from_fermenting inputs are 5 cucumbers + salt_dust (if not, BATCH-FAULT again: rerun with them) and its time; kimchi_from_onion 4 cabbage leaves + salt + onion. (2) read at 70 s: progress about 1400 (not 0). (3) 1 s after the swap: under 40. (4) at about 2000 ticks after the swap: no kimchi in slot 7. (5) at about 2420: 4 kimchi in slot 7

## SQ-STN-06 | FD pot plates from the remainder buffer: one bowl, five bowls, a bottle that never moves
> setblock 304 -60 340 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 306 -60 340 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 308 -60 342 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
pace 0
> setblock 304 -59 340 farmersdelight:cooking_pot{Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:6,id:"farmersdelight:vegetable_soup",Count:3b}]},ForgeCaps:{"creativedelight:remainder_buffer":{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:bowl",Count:1b}]}}}
> zc2 watch 304 -59 340 40 2
pace 1
sleep 4
pace 0
> setblock 306 -59 340 farmersdelight:cooking_pot{Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:6,id:"farmersdelight:vegetable_soup",Count:3b}]},ForgeCaps:{"creativedelight:remainder_buffer":{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:bowl",Count:5b}]}}}
> zc2 watch 306 -59 340 40 2
pace 1
sleep 4
pace 0
> setblock 308 -59 342 farmersdelight:cooking_pot{Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:6,id:"farmersdelight:vegetable_soup",Count:3b}]},ForgeCaps:{"creativedelight:remainder_buffer":{Items:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:glass_bottle",Count:1b}]}}}
> zc2 watch 308 -59 342 40 2
pace 1
sleep 4
reject \[zc2\] (watch )?error
look three watch series (t=0..40, the pots at x 304, 306, 308): one bowl: in the buffer about 10 ticks, then slot 7 about 10 ticks, then slot 8 holds 1 soup. Five bowls: 3 reach slot 7, 2 stay in the buffer, 3 soups plated. Bottle: never leaves the buffer, soup stays in slot 6. If t=0 already shows the end state, the console still lagged: judge on end states (c2a1 already showed them) and mark the timing half for a client CQ

